# Code owners for YapUI.
#
# This file is what makes `require_code_owner_review` on the `protect-main`
# ruleset mean anything — without it there is no owner to request, and the
# setting silently matches nothing.
#
# Effect, once `protect-main` carries `required_approving_review_count: 1` and
# `require_code_owner_review` (that settings change is applied when this PR
# lands — today the ruleset requires the two status checks but zero
# approvals): every pull request automatically requests a review from
# @Tatendaz and cannot merge until that review is approving. GitHub does not
# let anyone approve their own pull request, so a contribution always gets a
# second pair of eyes before it lands on `main`.

* @Tatendaz
